# kpl-core

Follow `AGENTS.md`. Product memory in `.kpl/specs/`; agent canon in `.kpl/agents/`.

## Token protocol

1. One skill (`.kpl/agents/skills/<name>/` or `.cursor/skills/<name>/` — same body)
2. `.kpl/memory/INDEX.md` → max 1–2 cards
3. Only current `.kpl/specs/features/<id>/` files needed
4. STANDARDS + pragmatic ladder — don't paste into chat
5. Product files ≥500 lines: Grep or Read with offset/limit; hook blocks → skill `bulk-read`

## Entries

`kpl-new-project` (no existing code) | `feature-discovery` (new capability/actor/route) | `fix-bug` (known files, no new capability/FR/trust boundary). Feature and fix share the same cycle and gates: Discover → PRD → specs+tasks → designer brief → mockups → branch → implement → security → publish. Fix differs only in branch prefix (`fix/`) and a mandatory root-cause field. Diff size does not choose the path. Scope change: edit PRD first.

## Branches

Never on `main`. Prefixes: `feature/` | `fix/` | `chore/`

## Architecture mentor

Present (brief, 3–4 lines) in all three entries, every non-trivial step: **Pattern / Why here / Tradeoff / Not doing**, then ask once if the user wants it expanded. Prefer boring. Ladder before layers.

Load skill `architecture-mentor` for the deep dive when crossing modules, auth, data ownership, trust boundaries, a new project's first ADR, or writing an ADR.

## Skills

Discover by description under `.cursor/skills/`. Index: `.kpl/specs/SKILLS.md`. Full practices: `.kpl/agents/rules/`.
